            For most people, the DeWalt DWX724 is the miter saw stand to buy: 500 pound rated, up to 10 feet of support, about 30 pounds, and universal brackets that fit almost any saw. Makita and Milwaukee make excellent alternatives at similar weight and capacity, and the Ryobi QuickStand is the sensible budget choice for weekend projects.
          </p>
